(National Cadet Corps \(NCC\) — Official Directorate General Training Notes) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. DOCTRINE OF FIELD SANITATION: Camp sanitation is the foundation of) Tj
T*
(preventive military medicine. Disease non-battle injuries \(DNBI\) have) Tj
T*
(historically incapacitated more soldiers than direct enemy action. Strict) Tj
T*
(enforcement of sanitation discipline prevents epidemic outbreaks in) Tj
T*
(temporary tented encampments and Combined Annual Training Camps \(CATC\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. SITING & PERIMETER REGULATIONS: Key camp layout regulations dictate that) Tj
T*
(field latrines and garbage disposal points must be located strictly) Tj
T*
(downwind from cadet living areas and at a minimum distance of 100 meters) Tj
T*
(away from natural drinking water sources and cookhouses/mess tents.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. FIELD LATRINE SPECIFICATIONS: For short-duration camps up to 3 days,) Tj
T*
(Shallow Trench Latrines \(STL\) are constructed measuring 3 feet long, 1 foot) Tj
T*
(wide, and 1.5 feet deep, covered with dry loose earth after each use. For) Tj
T*
(permanent camps lasting 10 to 14 days, Deep Trench Latrines \(DTL\) measuring) Tj
T*
(6 to 8 feet deep with fly-proof wooden squatter boxes are mandatory.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. WASTE DISPOSAL & VECTOR CONTROL: Organic waste must be incinerated daily) Tj
T*
(or buried in deep covered soakage pits. Regular spraying of lime powder and) Tj
T*
(permitted larvicides around wet areas prevents fly and mosquito breeding.) Tj
T*
() Tj
